use: mm.sdcard.socket
use: platform.linux.storage.bus
file: socket.cppm
---

# platform.linux.storage.socket

The storage-linux boards' SD socket as mm.sdcard.socket: mm.sdcard's SpiCard
on SPI 0 with chip select GPIO 23, the wiring platform.linux.storage.bus
gives the virtual card -- and rp2040_geek gives its TF socket, so a program
that mounts the socket reads the same on either.
